### Section 3 live demo: retries, circuit breaker, dead letters.
###
### Run the API, then walk this file top to bottom. Watch the console -- the
### interesting output is the "Pausing message listening" / "listener is
### latched" lines, not the HTTP responses.

@host = http://localhost:5199

### --- 1. Healthy baseline -------------------------------------------------
POST {{host}}/api/scheduling/faults
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mode": "None" }

###
POST {{host}}/api/scheduling/reset

### Fire 10. All 10 succeed.
POST {{host}}/api/scheduling/burst/10

###
GET {{host}}/api/scheduling/status


### --- 2. Transient failures: retries absorb them -------------------------
### 40% of calls now throw TechnicianOfflineException, which the handler's
### policy retries at 50ms, 250ms, then 1s.
POST {{host}}/api/scheduling/faults
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mode": "Flaky", "flakyPercentage": 40 }

###
POST {{host}}/api/scheduling/reset

### Fire 20. Attempts will exceed 20 -- that difference is the retries.
POST {{host}}/api/scheduling/burst/20

###
GET {{host}}/api/scheduling/status


### --- 3. Hard down: trip the circuit breaker -----------------------------
### Every call now throws SchedulingServiceDownException.
POST {{host}}/api/scheduling/faults
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mode": "Down" }

###
POST {{host}}/api/scheduling/reset

### Fire 40. Watch the console: the failure percentage crosses the threshold,
### the breaker trips, and the listener latches with the rest still queued.
POST {{host}}/api/scheduling/burst/40

### Attempts stop climbing even though messages are still waiting. That is the
### breaker doing its job -- not hammering a service that is clearly down.
GET {{host}}/api/scheduling/status


### --- 4. Recovery ---------------------------------------------------------
### Bring the service back. After the pause elapses the listener restarts and
### drains the backlog on its own. Nothing was lost.
POST {{host}}/api/scheduling/faults
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mode": "None" }

###
GET {{host}}/api/scheduling/status


### --- 5. Unretryable: discard, don't retry -------------------------------
### InvalidSchedulingRequestException can never succeed, so the policy
### discards it. Note the breaker EXCLUDES this exception -- a bad request is
### not evidence the service is unhealthy, and should not trip anything.
POST {{host}}/api/scheduling/faults
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mode": "Invalid" }

###
POST {{host}}/api/scheduling/burst/10

### Failures climb, but the listener keeps running.
GET {{host}}/api/scheduling/status


### --- 6. Hang: the execution timeout earns its keep ----------------------
### The service accepts the call and never returns. [MessageTimeout(5)]
### cancels the token, and the handler is interruptible because it passes that
### token all the way down.
POST {{host}}/api/scheduling/faults
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mode": "Hang" }

###
POST {{host}}/api/scheduling/burst/3

###
GET {{host}}/api/scheduling/status
